THOUGHT: I can see that when a table is initially created, both the grid columns and the cells have explicit widths set. But when we add a row later, if the grid columns don't have widths, the cells don't get widths either.

The fix should ensure that when adding a row, the cells get appropriate widths even when the grid columns don't have explicit widths. Looking at the initial table creation, I can see that cells get their width from the `col_width` parameter.

Let me modify the `add_row` method to handle this case properly:

```bash
sed -i '/for gridCol in tbl.tblGrid.gridCol_lst:/,/return _Row(tr, self)/{
    /for gridCol in tbl.tblGrid.gridCol_lst:/,/tc = tr.add_tc;/{
        /tc = tr.add_tc;/a\
            else:\
                # If grid column has no width, use default table cell width logic\
                # For now, we won't set a width which will let Word determine it
    }
}' src/docx/table.py
```

